            <ArticleTitle>Assessing progress on the NSF for coronary heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The government has produced a progress report that assesses the success of the National Service Framework on coronary heart disease published in 2000. The report shows that death rates for cardiovascular disease have fallen by 35%. The aim is to reduce the rate by 40% by 2010.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
